 "note": [
  "The English teen edition quotes the ASV in each chapter's epigraph; every French epigraph is the matching Segond (1910) text verbatim (whole verse, or the same portion the English quotes — Matthew 6:13 without Segond's doxology, 1 Samuel 2:8 to « trône de gloire »), with only French typographic spacing added, and the “(ASV)” label dropped. Psalm numbering shifts: Psalm 55:12-13 is cited « Psaume 55:13-14 » and Psalm 4:8 « Psaume 4:9 »; reference rows keep English numbering.",
  "The Matthew 6:13 epigraph is Segond (« délivre-nous du malin »), but Crowther's own echo and the prayer suggestion keep the familiar French Lord's Prayer « délivre-nous du mal » (self_rendered), matching the children's edition. In ch. 3 the body quotes Isaiah 61:1's Segond « pour proclamer aux captifs la liberté » (rather than Luke 4:18's « la délivrance ») because the text says Jesus read 'the verse at the top of this chapter'.",
  "Names and terms follow samuel-ajayi-crowther-a-life-children.fr: ship names unchanged (Myrmidon, Iphigenia, Pleiad, Dayspring); Cantorbéry; « Monseigneur » for 'My Lord' ('Right Reverend Bishop' → « Très Révérend Évêque »); « sept pence et demi »; « le Notre Père »; « Bonne nuit, papa ». Benue → « la Bénoué », Fulani → « peul », cowries → « cauris », Hannah kept with a gloss (« Anne, dans les Bibles françaises ») since the French Bible names Samuel's mother Anne. 'Over three hundred miles' → « plus de quatre cent cinquante kilomètres »; £1,000 → « mille livres ».",
  "Crowther's 1837–1891 letters and journal quotations are rendered in French from the English (no published French text was used). Title « Samuel Ajayi Crowther (Pour ados) » (34 chars) keeps the full name like the children's edition. AI-translated in-session; awaiting native review."
